// A bump arena for builder tools: cells allocated bottom up from one
// buffer in the data segment, a word holding how much of it is used, and
// running out a defined exit (docs/native-heap-arena-design.md §2, §3;
// issues/native-heap-arena.md).
//
// The arena is an ordinary `Source` buffer, so nothing here is new to the
// compiler: an allocation is a comparison and an add on the top word, a
// cell's fields are byte stores and loads, and running out branches to a
// statement the tool gives, which exits. A cell is named by its offset plus
// one, so the word 0 names no cell (`Nil`), and a name fits in four bytes
// for any arena the data segment holds (`io_data_limit`, 1 GiB).
//
// The compiler takes no shift yet (issues/function-ir-x86-shift-
// legalization.md), so a name's bytes cannot be cut out of its word cheaply:
// a loop testing bits is past one declaration's fuel in `write-elf`, and the
// same tests unrolled are past its memory. So a name the arena writes is
// kept as its bytes all along (`Name`): the next cell's name and the open
// payload's length are counted up a byte at a time with a carry, the way
// they grow, and a list's name is a copy of the next name taken when a
// cell is opened onto it. Reading a name back is cheap without shifts (each byte doubled
// into place), so a name read from a cell is a word. Names and lengths
// here have three bytes, which hold any arena up to 16 MiB; the fourth is
// zero.
//
// The cells a list is made of are laid out as `native_arena` says (a
// `List<List<BitVec(8)>>` cell: the next cell's name, the payload's length,
// then the payload's bytes), and only ever written while they are the top
// of the arena: a list is grown by consing a cell onto it, never changed
// in place. That is the discipline `native_arena`'s representation
// theorems speak of (`ArenaRef::cons_abs`, `ArenaRef::extend_abs`). Nothing
// here is proved: like every builder tool, an arena tool's meaning is the
// `Source` it lowers to, and `native_compile_correct` speaks of that.

import native_build;
import list;
import bitvec;
import bool;
import nat;

// A number below 2^24 kept as its three bytes, least significant first.
// No word holds the number beside them: every word a loop updates stays
// live across the loop, and what is live is what `write-elf`'s certificate
// pays for (docs/native-heap-arena-design.md §3.1), so where the number is
// wanted as a word the tool keeps it from what it knows (the top).
record Name { b0: Var, b1: Var, b2: Var }

// A name, zero, for the body.
fn name(body: Name → Act) → Act {
    local(num(0), λ b0 => local(num(0), λ b1 => local(num(0), λ b2 => body(Name(b0, b1, b2)))))
}

// One name made the other.
fn Name::copy(self to: Name, from: Name) → Act {
    to.b0.set(from.b0.get()) ++ to.b1.set(from.b1.get()) ++ to.b2.set(from.b2.get())
}

fn Name::clear(self n: Name) → Act {
    n.b0.set(num(0)) ++ n.b1.set(num(0)) ++ n.b2.set(num(0))
}

// The name grown by `k` (below 256), the carry going up a byte at a time.
fn Name::bump(self n: Name, k: Nat) → Act {
    n.b0.set(n.b0.get() + num(k))
    ++ when(n.b0.get().below(num(256)).not(),
        n.b0.set(n.b0.get() - num(256)) ++ n.b1.set(n.b1.get() + num(1))
        ++ when(n.b1.get().equals(num(256)), n.b1.set(num(0)) ++ n.b2.set(n.b2.get() + num(1))))
}

// The buffer the cells live in; the word holding how many of its bytes are
// used; the name the next cell would get (the top plus one); and the length
// of the open cell's payload so far.
record Arena { buf: Buf, top: Var, next: Name, length: Name }

// The arena empty, for the body.
fn with_arena(buf: Buf, body: Arena → Act) → Act {
    local(num(0), λ top => name(λ next => name(λ length =>
        next.bump(1) ++ body(Arena(buf, top, next, length)))))
}

// Its bytes free.
fn Arena::room(self a: Arena) → Val { a.buf.size() - a.top.get() }

// One byte stored at the top, the open cell's payload growing by one;
// `full` if none is free. `full` is expected to exit.
fn Arena::push(self a: Arena, byte: Val, full: Act) → Act {
    branch(a.room().below(num(1)), full,
        a.buf.put(a.top.get(), byte) ++ a.top.set(a.top.get() + num(1)) ++ a.next.bump(1) ++ a.length.bump(1))
}

// A name's four bytes at offset `at`.
fn Arena::put_name(self a: Arena, at: Val, n: Name) → Act {
    local(at, λ p => a.buf.put(p.get(), n.b0.get()) ++ a.buf.put(p.get() + num(1), n.b1.get())
        ++ a.buf.put(p.get() + num(2), n.b2.get()) ++ a.buf.put(p.get() + num(3), num(0)))
}

// The word doubled `n` times: a shift left by `n`, as additions, in a loop
// (so the statement is small for the compiler however large `n` is).
fn doubled(t: Var, n: Nat) → Act {
    local(num(n), λ left => loop_while(left.get(), t.set(t.get() + t.get()) ++ left.set(left.get() - num(1))))
}

// The number a name's three bytes at offset `at` hold, into `into`: the
// high byte first, doubled into place by each byte below it.
fn Arena::get_name(self a: Arena, at: Val, into: Var) → Act {
    local(at, λ p =>
        into.set(a.buf.at(p.get() + num(2))) ++ doubled(into, 8)
        ++ into.set(into.get() + a.buf.at(p.get() + num(1))) ++ doubled(into, 8)
        ++ into.set(into.get() + a.buf.at(p.get())))
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Lists of byte strings (`native_arena`'s line cells)

// A cell's offset, from its name.
fn cell_at(cell: Val) → Val { cell - num(1) }

// The cell after this one, and the length of its payload, into `into`;
// where its payload starts.
fn Arena::next_of(self a: Arena, cell: Val, into: Var) → Act { a.get_name(cell_at(cell), into) }
fn Arena::length_of(self a: Arena, cell: Val, into: Var) → Act { a.get_name(cell_at(cell) + num(4), into) }
fn Arena::payload(self a: Arena, cell: Val) → Val { cell_at(cell) + num(8) }

// A cell opened at the top onto the list `list` (its name's bytes, and the
// name as a word in `head`), which it then heads: its header (the list's
// name and a zero length) written, its payload empty, and `list` and `head`
// made its name. Bytes `push`ed after it are its payload until it is
// closed. `full` if the header has no room.
fn Arena::open_cell(self a: Arena, list: Name, head: Var, full: Act) → Act {
    branch(a.room().below(num(8)), full,
        a.put_name(a.top.get(), list)
        ++ a.put_name(a.top.get() + num(4), a.length)
        ++ list.copy(a.next) ++ head.set(a.top.get() + num(1))
        ++ a.top.set(a.top.get() + num(8)) ++ a.next.bump(8))
}

// The open cell, named `cell`, closed: its payload's length (what was
// pushed since it opened) written, and the count started again.
fn Arena::close_cell(self a: Arena, cell: Val) → Act {
    a.put_name(cell_at(cell) + num(4), a.length) ++ a.length.clear()
}

// The body on each cell of the list from `list`, first to last, with the
// length of the cell's payload. A list grown by consing at the top of the
// arena (`read_lines`'s) lies in it newest first and cell against cell, so
// a cell's payload ends where the cell before it in the list starts, and the
// first one's at the top: its length is read off where the walk has been,
// with no name read back from the cell.
fn Arena::each(self a: Arena, list: Val, body: Var → Var → Act) → Act {
    local(list, λ p => local(a.top.get(), λ end => local(num(0), λ len => loop_while(p.get(),
        len.set(end.get() - a.payload(p.get())) ++ body(p, len)
        ++ end.set(cell_at(p.get())) ++ a.next_of(p.get(), p)))))
}
